  {"tool": "text_apply_char_style", "args": {"frame_id": "${title.frame_id}", "start": 0, "end": 1, "baseline": "superscript"}, "note": "baseline is \"normal\", \"superscript\", \"subscript\" or {\"shift\": points} (positive raises). Super and subscript use the font's own OS/2 size and offset, else 58% size and a 33% shift. A raised run makes its line taller; the story text is unchanged."},
  {"tool": "text_apply_char_style", "args": {"frame_id": "${title.frame_id}", "start": 2, "end": 8, "caps": "small", "strikethrough": true, "ligatures": false, "kerning": false}, "note": "caps is \"none\", \"small\" or \"all\" (display only; the characters stay as typed). Small caps use the font's smcp feature when it has one, else lowercase letters are drawn as capitals at 70% size. ligatures and kerning default on."},
  {"tool": "text_apply_char_style", "args": {"frame_id": "${title.frame_id}", "start": 0, "end": 8, "baseline": {"shift": -2.5}, "caps": "none", "strikethrough": false, "ligatures": true, "kerning": true}, "note": "A custom baseline shift of 2.5 pt down, and every other attribute back to its default."},
  {"tool": "text_apply_char_style", "args": {"frame_id": "${title.frame_id}", "start": 0, "end": 8, "baseline": "normal"}},
